            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds#KhavkineSchreiber17"}> Khavkine-Schreiber 17, example 3.4
            )
          %p
            For more on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            from the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds"} geometry of physics – manifolds and orbifolds
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#Supergeometry
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion+fields"} fermion fields
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
          %p
            Field theories of interest crucially involve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+fields"} fermionic fields
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FermionicBosonicFields"}
            below), such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldBundle"}
            below), which are subject to the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+exclusion+principle"}> Pauli exclusion principle
            ”, a key reason for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stability+of+matter"} stability of matter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundles"} field bundles
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+fiber"} field fiber
            is not an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            (more on this in remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianDensityOfDiracFieldSupergeometricNature"}
            and remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupergeometricNatureOfDiracEquation"}
            below).
          %p
            This “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"}> supergeometry
            ” is an immediate generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} infinitesimal geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalGeometry"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal"} infinitesimal
            elements in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            may be equipped with a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} grading
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
          %p
            The “super”-terminology for something as down-to-earth as the mathematical principle behind the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stability+of+matter"} stability of matter
            may seem unfortunate. For better or worse, this terminology has become standard since the middle of the 20th century. But the concept that today is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            was in fact first considered by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ausdehnungslehre"} Grassmann 1844
            who got it right (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ausdehnungslehre"}> Ausdehnungslehre
            ”) but apparently was too far ahead of his time and remained unappreciated.
          %p
            Beware that considering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            does
            %em not
            necessarily involve considering “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"}> supersymmetry
            ”. Supergeometry is the geometry of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion+fields"} fermion fields
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FermionicBosonicFields"}
            below), and that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            fields in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            are fermionic has been
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimentally
            established since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stern-Gerlach+experiment"} Stern-Gerlach experiment
            in 1922. Supersymmetry, on the other hand, is a hypothetical extension of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            within the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry"} geometry of physics – supersymmetry
          #SupercommutativeSuperalgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"}> supercommutative superalgebra
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              together with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              decomposition of its underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi even
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} A_{even} \oplus A_{odd}
                    \\,,
            %p
              such that the product in the algebra respects the multiplication in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+2"} group of order 2
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi even
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2 = \{even, odd\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi even
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi even
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi odd
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi odd
                      %mo }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi even
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi odd
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi even
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi even
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi odd
                      %mo }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left.
                    \\array{
                    A_{even} \cdot A_{even}
                    \\\
                    A_{odd} \cdot A_{odd}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\subset A_{even}
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    \\left.
                    \\array{
                    A_{odd} \cdot A_{even}
                    \\\
                    A_{even} \cdot A_{odd}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\subset A_{odd}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              if for all elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1, a_2 \in A
              which are of homogeneous degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi even
                    %mo ,
                    %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert a_i \vert} \in \mathbb{Z}/2 = \{even, odd\}
              in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_i \in A_{{\vert a_i\vert}} \subset A
            %p we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_1 \cdot a_2 = (-1)^{{\vert a_1 \vert \vert a_2 \vert}} a_2 \cdot a_1
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebras"} superalgebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; A \longrightarrow A'
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              such that the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} grading
              is respected in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi even
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi even
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f(A_{even}) \subset A'_{even}
                    \\phantom{AAAAA}
                    f(A_{odd}) \subset A'_{odd}
                    \\,.
          %p
            For more details on superalgebra see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+superalgebra"} geometry of physics – superalgebra
          #GrassmannAlgebra.num_example
            %h6#example_21 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (basic examples of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
            %p
              Basic examples of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  becomes a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
                  by declaring it to be all in even degree:
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi even
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = A_{even}
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≔
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \coloneqq \wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}} V^\ast
                  is a supercommutative superalgebra with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi even
                        %mo ≔
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi even
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{even} \coloneqq \wedge^{even} V^\ast
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi odd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msup
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi odd
                          %msup
                            %mi V
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{odd} \coloneqq \wedge^{odd} V^\ast
                %p
                  More explicitly, if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{R}^s
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                  with canonical dual
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\theta^i)_{i = 1}^s
                  then the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi s
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet (\mathbb{R}^s)^\ast
                  is the real algebra which is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
                  from the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta^i
                  regarded in odd degree and hence subject to the relation
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi j
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\theta^i \cdot \theta^j = - \theta^j \cdot \theta^i
                        \\,.
                %p
                  In particular this implies that all the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta^i
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal"} infinitesimal
                  (def.
                  = succeed "):" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimallyThickendSmoothManifold"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\theta^i \cdot \theta^i = 0
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
                  two
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras"} tensor product
                  supercommutative superalgebra
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi ℝ
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} A_2
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                  with ordinary algebra of smooth functions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
                  regarded as a supercommutative superalgebra by the first example above, the tensor product with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
                  (second example above) is the supercommutative superalgebta
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi ℝ
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        C^\infty(X) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \wedge^\bullet((\mathbb{R}^s)\ast)
                %p whose elements may uniquely be expanded in the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi j
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi j
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi s
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi s
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f + f_i \theta^i + f_{i j} \theta^i \theta^j + f_{i j k} \theta^i \theta^j \theta^k + \cdots + f_{i_1 \cdots i_s} \theta^{i_1} \cdots \theta^{i_s}
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{i_1 \cdots i_k} \in C^\infty(X)
                  are smooth functions on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  which are skew-symmetric in their indices.
          %p
            The following is the direct super-algebraic analog of the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+smooth+manifolds"} infinitesimally thickened Cartesian spaces
            (def.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimallyThickendSmoothManifold"}
          #SuperCartesianSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"}> super Cartesian space
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
              is represented by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-commutative+superalgebra"} super-commutative superalgebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"}> super vector space
              ) is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} \langle 1 \rangle \oplus V
            %p
              of the 1-dimensional even vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle 1 \rangle = \mathbb{R}
              of multiples of 1, with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              that is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in that for each element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in V
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a^{n+1} = 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              More generally, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \times Spec(A)
              is represented by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-commutative+algebra"} super-commutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \otimes A \in \mathbb{R} Alg
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras"} tensor product of algebras
              of the algebra of smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              on an actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              of some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} \langle 1\rangle \oplus V
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrassmannAlgebra"}
            %p
              Specifically, for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in \mathbb{N}
            #eq:StandardSuperpoints.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Spec
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0 \vert s}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    Spec\left(  \wedge^\bullet (\mathbb{R}^s)^\ast \right)
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
              is by definition the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\theta^i)_{i = 1}^s
              in odd degree (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrassmannAlgebra"}
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi b
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi b
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Spec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi s
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Spec
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi ℝ
                              %msup
                                %mo ∧
                                %mo •
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi s
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{b\vert s}
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\mathbb{R}^b \times \mathbb{R}^{0 \vert s}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\mathbb{R}^b \times Spec( \wedge^\bullet(\mathbb{R}^s)^\ast )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Spec\left(  C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^b) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \wedge^\bullet (\mathbb{R}^s)^\ast  \right)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              for the corresponding super Cartesian spaces whose algebra of functions is as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrassmannAlgebra"}
            %p
              We say that a
              %em smooth function
              between two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1} \times Spec(A_1) \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{R}^{n_2} \times Spec(A_2)
            %p
              is by definition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} dually
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_1}) \otimes A_1
                    \\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_2}) \otimes A_2
                    \\,.
          #SuperpointInducedByFiniteDimensionalVectorSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_22 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
                induced by a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^\ast
              denoting its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V^\ast
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              that it generates. This being a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+algebra"} supercommutative algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
            %p We denote this superpoint by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi odd
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi dim
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_{odd} \simeq \mathbb{R}^{0 \vert dim(V)}
                    \\,.
          %p
            All the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            that we discussed
            %a{:href => "#Geometry"} above
            generalizes immediately to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} super sign rule
            which says that whenever two odd-graded elements swap places, a minus sign is picked up. In particular we have the following generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsAndCartanCalculus"} above
          #DifferentialFormOnSuperCartesianSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition_13 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{b\vert s}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{b\vert s})
                    \\;=\;
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^b) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \wedge^\bullet \mathbb{R}^s
            %p
              with canonical even-graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mn 1
                          %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^i)_{i = 1^b}
              and odd-graded coordinate functions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mi j
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\theta^j)_{j = 1}^s
            %p
              Then the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{b\vert s}
              is, in super-generalization of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialnForms"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutative+algebra"} graded commutative algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet(\mathbb{R}^{b|s})
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{b|s})
                    \\otimes_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\wedge^\bullet \langle
                    d x^1, \cdots, d x^b,
                    \\;
                    d \theta^1, \cdots, d\theta^s
                    \\rangle
            %p
              which is generated over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{b\vert s})
              from new generators
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi i
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mtext deg
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi θ
                            %mi j
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mtext deg
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{deg} = (1,even)
                    }{\underbrace{ d x^i }}
                    \\phantom{AAAAA}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{deg} = (1,odd)
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    d \theta^j
                    }
                    }
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              is defined in degree-0 by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi j
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d f
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\frac{\partial f}{\partial x^i} d x^i
                    +
                    \\frac{\partial f}{\partial \theta^j} d \theta^j
            %p
              and extended from there as a bigraded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              of bi-degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#deRhamDifferential"}
            %p
              Accordingly, the operation of contraction with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector+fields"} tangent vector fields
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContractionOfFormsWithVectorFields"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1,\sigma)
              if the tangent vector has super-degree
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th generator
                  %th bi-degree
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} x^a
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (0,even)
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %msup
                            %mi θ
                            %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} \theta^\alpha
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (0,odd)
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %msup
                            %mi dx
                            %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} dx^a
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (1,even)
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi θ
                            %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} d\theta^\alpha
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (1,odd)
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th derivation
                  %th bi-degree
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mi d
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} d
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (1,even)
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}\iota_{\partial x^a}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (-1, even)
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %msup
                                %mi θ
                                %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}\iota_{\partial \theta^\alpha}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} (-1,odd)
            %p
              This means that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \Omega^\bullet(\mathbb{R}^{b\vert s})
              is in bidegree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_\alpha, \sigma_\alpha)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in \Omega^\bullet(\mathbb{R}^{b \vert \sigma})
              is in bidegree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi β
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_\beta, \sigma_\beta)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi β
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi α
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi β
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi α
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi β
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha \wedge \beta
                    \\;
                    \=
                    \\;
                    (- 1)^{n_\alpha n_\beta + \sigma_\alpha \sigma_\beta}
                    \\;
                    \\beta \wedge \alpha
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence there are
              %em two
              contributions to the sign picked up when exchanging two super-differential forms in the wedge product:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there is a “cohomological sign” which for commuting an
                  = succeed "-forms" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_1
                  = succeed "-form" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_2
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi n
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mi n
                                %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{n_1 n_2}
              %li
                %p
                  in addition there is a “super-grading” sign which for commuting a
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_2
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\sigma_1 \sigma_2}
            %p For example:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x^{a_1} (dx^{a_2}) \;=\; + (dx^{a_2}) x^{a_1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta^\alpha (dx^a) \;=\; + (dx^a) \theta^\alpha
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta^{\alpha_1} (d\theta^{\alpha_2})
                    \\;=\;
                    \- (d\theta^{\alpha_2}) \theta^{\alpha_1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dx^{a_1}
                    \\wedge
                    d x^{a_2}
                    \\;=\;
                    \-
                    d x^{a_2}
                    \\wedge
                    d x^{a_1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi dx
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dx^a
                    \\wedge
                    d \theta^{\alpha}
                    \\;=\;
                    \-
                    d\theta^{\alpha}
                    \\wedge
                    d x^a
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d\theta^{\alpha_1}
                    \\wedge
                    d \theta^{\alpha_2}
                    \\;=\;
                    +
                    d\theta^{\alpha_2}
                    \\wedge
                    d \theta^{\alpha_1}
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "signs+in+supergeometry#CastellaniDAuriaFre91"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91 (II.2.106) and (II.2.109)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "signs+in+supergeometry#DeligneFreed99"} Deligne-Freed 99, section 6
          %p
            Beware that there is also
            %em another
            sign rule for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            used in the literature. See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
            for further discussion.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            It is clear now by direct analogy with the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSet"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
            generalization is. For definiteness we spell it out yet once more:
          #SuperFormalSmoothSet.num_defn
            %h6#definition_14 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"}> super smooth set
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} super smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \times Spec(A)
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X(\mathbb{R}^n \times Spec(A)) \in Set
                %p
                  to be called the set of
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  or
                  %em plots
                  from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \times Spec(A)
                  to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \times Spec(A_1) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n_2} \times Spec(A_2)
                  between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
                  a choice of function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f^\ast \;\colon\; X(\mathbb{R}^{n_2} \times Spec(A_2)) \longrightarrow X(\mathbb{R}^{n_1} \times Spec(A_1))
                %p to be thought of as the precomposition operation
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi n
                                %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi Φ
                          %mi X
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mover
                          %mo ↦
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
