                    Hom_{\mathbb{R}Vect}( V^\ast\,,\, C^\infty(U)_{odd} ) \,\times\, Hom_{\mathbb{R}Vect}( V^\ast, C^\infty(U)_{even} )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    V_{odd}(U) \times V(U)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    (V_{odd} \times V)(U)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here in the third line we used that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V^\ast
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              on its generators in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
              out of the Grassmann algebra is uniquely fixed by the underlying degree-preserving
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
              on these generators. Since in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              all the generators are in odd degree, this is equivalently a linear map from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^\ast
              to the odd-graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              underlying
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(U)[\theta](\theta^2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi odd
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(U)_{odd} \oplus C^\infty(U)_{even}\langle \theta \rangle
            %p
              Then in the fourth line we used that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+coproduct"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of linear maps into the direct summands.
            %p
              That all these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural
              means that they are compatible with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to U'
              and therefore this says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}, V_{odd}]
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi odd
                    %mo ×
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{odd} \times V
              are the same as seen by super-smooth plots, hence that they are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} super smooth sets
          %p
            With this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            in hand we finally turn to defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            species:
          #DiracFieldBundle.num_example
            %h6#example_27 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
                for
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinkowskiSpacetime"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2+1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3+1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5+1
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 9
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 9+1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              from prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpinorRepsByNormedDivisionAlgebra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mn 2
                              %mo ⊕
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mn 2
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℂ
                                %mn 2
                              %mo ⊕
                              %msup
                                %mi ℂ
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mn 3
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℍ
                                %mn 2
                              %mo ⊕
                              %msup
                                %mi ℍ
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mn 5
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi 𝕆
                                %mn 2
                              %mo ⊕
                              %msup
                                %mi 𝕆
                                %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo =
                              %mn 9
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S \;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^2 \oplus \mathbb{R}^2 &amp; \vert &amp; p + 1 = 2+1
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{C}^2 \oplus \mathbb{C}^2  &amp;\vert&amp; p + 1 = 3 + 1
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{H}^2 \oplus \mathbb{H}^2 &amp;\vert&amp; p + 1 = 5 + 1
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{O}^2  \oplus \mathbb{O}^2 &amp;\vert&amp; p + 1 = 9 + 1
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p With
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi dim
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_{odd} \simeq \mathbb{R}^{0 \vert dim(S)}
            %p
              the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperpointInducedByFiniteDimensionalVectorSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              for the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                    %mi Σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \;\coloneqq\; \Sigma \times S_{odd} \overset{pr_1}{\to} \Sigma
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+fiber"} field fiber
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi odd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{odd}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %p
              The traditional two-component
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
              basis from remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoComponentSpinorNotation"}
              provides
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+field"} fermionic field
              coordinates (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FermionicBosonicFields"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+fiber"} field fiber
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi odd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{odd}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi A
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ξ
                          %mrow
                            %mo †
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo ˙
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo ˙
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\psi^A
                    \\right)_{A = 1}^4
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    (\chi_a), (\xi^{\dagger \dot a})
                    \\right)_{a,\dot a = 1,2}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that these are
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K} = \mathbb{C}
              then each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_a
              in turn has two components, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
              and an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
            %p
              A key point with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldBundle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi^A)
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ξ
                        %mrow
                          %mo †
                          %mover
                            %mi a
                            %mo ˙
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left((\chi_a), (\xi^{\dagger \dot a})\right)
              are now odd-graded elements in the function algebra on the field fiber, which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(S_{odd}) =  \wedge^\bullet(S^\ast)
            #eq:DiracFieldCoordinatesAnticommute.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi α
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi β
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi^\alpha  \psi^{\beta} = - \psi^{\beta} \psi^\alpha
                    \\,.
            %p
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DermisekAnticommutingSpinorFieldCoordinates.jpg", :width => "400"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                snippet grabbed from (
                %a{:href => "Dirac+field#DermisekI8"}> Dermisek 09
                )
          %p
            We analyze the special nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            a little (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            (remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldSupergeometric"}
            below)
          #DiracSpaceOfFieldHistories.num_defn
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
                of the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \Sigma \times S_{odd} \overset{pr_1}{\to}  \Sigma
              be the super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FermionicBosonicFields"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
              from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldBundle"}
            %p
              Then the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi SuperSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S_{odd})
                    \\;\in\;
                    SuperSmoothSet
            %p
              from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupergeometricSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              has the following properties:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \mathbb{R}^n
                  an ordinary
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                  (with no super-geometric thickening, def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
                  = succeed "-parameterized" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mn 0
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Psi_{(-)}\;\colon\;\mathbb{R}^n \overset{ 0 }{\longrightarrow} \Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S_{odd})
                %p
                  and this corresponds to the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+section"} zero section
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Psi^A_{(-)} = 0
                        \\,.
              %li#OddParameterizedFieldHistories
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \mathbb{R}^{n \vert 1}
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
                  (
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}>
                  ) with a single super-odd dimension, then
                  = succeed "-parameterized" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Φ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Phi_{(-)} \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^{n\vert 1} \longrightarrow \Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S_{odd})
                %p
                  are in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                  with plots of sections of the
                  = succeed "-field" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+field"} bosonic
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi even
                        %mo =
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{even} = S
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
                  regarded as an ordinary vector space:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Psi_{(-)} \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S_{even})
                        \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, these two kinds of plots determine the fermionic field space completely: It is in fact
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperpointInducedByFiniteDimensionalVectorSpace"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_\Sigma(\Sigma \times S_{odd})
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\left(
                    \\Gamma_\Sigma(E\times S_{even})
                    \\right)_{odd}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              In the first case, the plot is a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperCartesianSpace"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^{p,1} \longrightarrow S_{odd}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By definitions this is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} dually
              homomorphism of real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^{p,1})
                    \\longleftarrow
                    \\wedge^\bullet S^\ast
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the ordinary algebras of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
            %p For the second case, notice that a morphism of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Φ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n\vert 1}
                    \\overset{\Phi_{(-)}}{\longrightarrow}
                    S_{odd}
            %p
              is by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentBundleOdd"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} naturally identified
              with a morphism of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi odd
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi even
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\overset{\Psi_{(-)}}{\longrightarrow}
                    [\mathbb{R}^{0 \vert 1}, S_{odd}]
                    \\simeq
                    S_{odd} \times S_{even}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the identification on the right is from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperpointsMapping"}
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} nature
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              these morphisms in turn are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} naturally identified
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of morphisms of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi n
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi S
                                %mi odd
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi n
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi S
                                %mi even
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^n &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; S_{odd}\,,
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^n &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; S_{even}
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now, as in the first point above, here the first component is uniquely fixed to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi odd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \overset{0}{\to} S_{odd}
          #DiracFieldSupergeometric.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
                nature of the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            %p
              Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              how two basic facts about the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  On the one hand a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+history"} field history
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
                  is
                  %em not
                  an ordinary section of an ordinary
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^A
                  anti-commute with each other, which is not the case for ordinary functions, and this is crucial for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                  of the Dirac field to be well defined, we come to this below in example
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianDensityForDiracField"}
              %li
                %p
                  On the other hand a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+history"} field history
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
                  is supposed to be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  of a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %p
              Therefore prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              serves to shows how, even though a Dirac field is not defined to be an ordinary section of an ordinary vector bundle, it is nevertheless encoded by such an ordinary section: One says that this ordinary section is a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"}> superfield
              \-component” of the Dirac field, the one linear in a Grassmann variable
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This concludes our discussion of the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            itself. In the
            %a{:href => "#FieldVariations"} following chapter
            we consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            of fields.
